  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "mdAT 2.0: framework-independent core. Own JSON comparison engine (no xunit/Quibble dependency), ignoreArrayOrder option, net8.0/net9.0/net10.0. In the markdown files: a test case is named Method_Title@file.md; the test explorer points each case to its title in the markdown file (or to the start of its document in a YAML file); each markdown test file keeps a link to its C# test; a case marked skipped is listed and reported as ignored, and when a case is marked selected the other cases of the file stay in the list, ignored; a case can have categories and properties (category=Smoke,Fast priority=High in the line of its code block, tags: in the front matter of the file); a JsonDocument or JsonElement whose root is a string holding a JSON object or array is written as that object or array again (mdAT 1.4 behaviour); the file of generateExpectedData is written again when another process is using it. See the migration section of the README.",
